form\nL199: \nL200: crystals and lumps\nL201: \nL202: ### reaction suitability\nL203: \nL204: core: cerium, reagent type: inorganic catalyst\nL205: \nL206: ### impurities\nL207: \nL208: 1-2% La\nL209: \nL210: ### SMILES string\nL211: \nL212: [Ce+3].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[O-][N+]([O-])=O.[O-][N+]([O-])=O.[O-][N+]([O-])=O\nL213: \nL214: ### InChI\nL215: \nL216: 1S/Ce.3NO3.6H2O/c;3*2-1(3)4;;;;;;/h;;;;6*1H2/q+3;3*-1;;;;;;\nL217: \nL218: ### InChI key\nL219: \nL220: QQZMWMKOWKGPQY-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL221: \nL222: Description\nL223: ### General description\nL224: \nL225: Cerium (III) nitrate hexahydrate is the most common form of cerium nitrate. It is a white-to-yellow crystalline salt, and it is highly soluble in water, alcohol, and acetone, although solutions can appear slightly hazy. Like many trivalent metal nitrates, cerium (III) nitrate hexahydrate has a low-melting point of only 57 °C and thermally decomposes at low temperatures too, beginning at 190 °C and proceeding rapidly at 280 °C with complete decomposition at 390-400 °C.\nL226: ### Application\nL227: Cerium (III) nitrate hexahydrate is widely used as a source of cerium, especially in the synthesis of micro- or nano-structured ceria (cerium oxide). Because of its high solubility and low decomposition temperature, cerium (III) nitrate hexahydrate is an ideal reagent for hydrothermal reactions, sol-gel processing, and co-precipitation and calcination reactions.\nL228: Ceria is one of the best studied materials-platforms for catalysis and solid oxide fuel cells. Consequently scientists have developed well-controlled synthetic protocols using cerium (III) nitrate hexahydrate for preparing ceria nanoparticles including nano cubes, nanotubes, and nanorods.\nL229: The tailorable synthesis facilitates using ceria as a catalyst support, for example leveraging the porosity of the microstructure to impregnate metals and metal alloys, or for example synthesizing ceria-based materials like ceria-zirconia.\nL230: * * *\nL231: ## Compare Similar Items\nL232: \nL233: 【18†View Full Comparison】\nL234: \nL235: * * *\nL236: \nL237: Show Differences\nL238: \nL239: [Input]\nL240: \nL241: 1 of 1\nL242: ###### This Item\nL243:  | 202991  | 392219  | 325503\nL244: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL245: 【19†Sigma-Aldrich 238538 Cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich 202991 Cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【21†Sigma-Aldrich 392219 Cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【22†Sigma-Aldrich 325503 Cerium(III) carbonate hydrate】[Button: Quick View]\nL246: description 99% trace metals basis  | description 99.999% trace metals basis  | description 99.99% trace metals basis  | description 99.9% trace metals basis\nL247: form crystals and lumps  | form crystals and lumps  | form crystals and lumps  | form powder\nL248: assay 99% trace metals basis  | assay 99.999% trace metals basis  | assay 99.99% trace metals basis  | assay 99.9% trace metals basis\nL249: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 100  | Quality Level 100  | Quality Level 100\nL250: impurities 1-2% La  | impurities≤15.0 ppm Trace Metal Analysis  | impurities≤150.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis  | impurities≤1500.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis\nL251: reaction suitability reagent type: catalyst  | reaction suitability core: cerium, reagent type: catalyst  | reaction suitability core: cerium, reagent type: catalyst  | reaction suitability reagent type: catalyst, core: cerium\nL252: * * *\nL253: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL254: \nL255: Explore all of our products under 【23†Cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】\nL256: \nL257: 【23†View All Products】\nL258: \nL259: * * *\nL260: \nL261: ## Safety Information\nL262: \nL263: ### Pictograms\nL264: \nL265: 【24†GHS05,GHS09】\nL266: \nL267: ### Signal Word\nL268: \nL269: Danger\nL270: \nL271: ### Hazard Codes\nL272: \nL273: 【25†H318,H410】\nL274: \nL275: ### Precautionary Statements\nL276: \nL277: 【26†P273 - P280 -